Inspect, cancel and delete generation jobs.

This is the resume path for `azd ai eval generate`: a job started with --no-wait, or one whose client was interrupted, is reattached to here rather than restarted.

Pass --dataset or --evaluator to say which generation to act on. The two are separate service collections, so it is required.

Usage
  azd ai eval job [command]

Available Commands
  cancel : Cancel an in-flight generation job.
  delete : Delete a generation job record.
  list   : List the project's generation jobs.
  show   : Show a generation job, and collect its artifact once it has finished.

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for job
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
  List dataset generation jobs
    azd ai eval job list --dataset

Use azd ai eval job [command] --help to view examples and more information about a specific command.
